From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Attard <sattard@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:02:58 +0000
Subject: test: drop removed wasm rab integration flag

Chromium's V8 shipped resizable ArrayBuffer / WebAssembly integration and
removed the --experimental-wasm-rab-integration flag, so passing it makes
the test exit with "bad option". Node.js v24.22.0 added the flag to
test-internal-webidl-buffer-source.js.

This patch can be removed once Node.js's bundled V8 no longer has the
flag and the test stops passing it.

Refs: https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/65845
Refs: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/7708297

diff --git a/test/parallel/test-internal-webidl-buffer-source.js b/test/parallel/test-internal-webidl-buffer-source.js
index b3158bd7d3481e3257fc97a1ed584cd27e8d0c9b..8e81f42a9456054d95dd60fca6c99f4ebcf21736 100644
--- a/test/parallel/test-internal-webidl-buffer-source.js
+++ b/test/parallel/test-internal-webidl-buffer-source.js
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-// Flags: --expose-internals --experimental-wasm-rab-integration
+// Flags: --expose-internals
 'use strict';
 
 const common = require('../common');
